      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe a 24-year-old man who presented with unilateral sacroiliac pain associated with constitutional symptoms. Subsequent biopsy and pathohistologic evaluation demonstrated Ewing's sarcoma. We emphasize a consideration of Ewing's sarcoma in the differential diagnosis of unilateral sacroiliac pain."},
